{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Woe is me</b> — the prophet's word is in the mouth of the maskil (the discerning one) at that time, and it is 'my people,' who are mentioned." "<b>As the gleanings of summer</b> — like: my holy things, that which the poor gather from the late fruit, and this is by way of analogy, as though there is no righteous one."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:11.456763872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}